    "pmc10241557_l172_l175_deucravacitinib_cd3_tyk2": "L172-L175:Deucravacitinib (BMS-986165, NICE TA907) is the first approved de novo deuterated drug; its -CD3 deuterium switch suppresses metabolic N-demethylation to non-selective JH1/JAK1-3 metabolites while binding allosterically to the TYK2 JH2 pseudokinase domain, avoiding pan-JAK MACE/VTE black-box risks.",
    "pmc6260175_l1_pmc7385579_l1_l5_nudt15_r139c": "L1-L5:NUDT15 p.Arg139Cys (NUDT15*3, rs116855232) unfolds the alpha2 helix of human NUDT15 diphosphatase (PDB: 5LPG) and strongly predisposes Asian IBD and autoimmune patients to severe thiopurine-induced leukopenia and neutropenic sepsis missed by TPMT-only testing.",
    "pmc8466143_l50_l51_pmc9472599_l38_nv_fnd_selfia": "L50-L51:Fluorescent nanodiamonds (FNDs) hosting spin-1 NV- colour centres modulated by a 2.87 GHz microwave field separate biological autofluorescence background, providing 10^5 times higher lateral-flow sensitivity than colloidal gold and single-copy (82 zM) HIV-1 RNA / SARS-CoV-2 variant detection.",
    "pmc9924091_l1_l8_pmc9425786_l1_l7_nirmatrelvir_mpro": "L1-L8:Nirmatrelvir (PF-07321332, NICE TA878) reacts reversibly via its electrophilic nitrile warhead with nucleophilic Cys145 of SARS-CoV-2 Mpro (PDB: 7RFS, 1.804 A thioimidate C-S bond) and requires ritonavir CYP3A4 boosting (-88.9% hospitalization risk in EPIC-HR, with severe CYP3A4 DDI hazards)."
